From cade893ffe30ababede364f294a90347424daadb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 14:38:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(deepseek-v4.1): decode rows keep the decode attention
 kernel in batch-invariant mode

Replaces running every decode row single-pass. A step's attention mode came
from its longest query, so decode rows that shared a step with prompt rows ran
the single-pass extend kernel while decode-only steps ran the split decode
kernel, which rounds differently; forcing single-pass everywhere cost about
1.3 ms per decode step. With VLLM_DS41_BATCH_INVARIANT=1:

- the step kind comes from request state (CommonAttentionMetadata.is_prefilling):
  a step holding prompt rows is never a decode step, even when its queries are
  as short as a decode step's (the last token of a fully cached prompt);
- such a step reports its leading decode rows, and every layer runs them on
  the decode plan and the remaining rows single-pass, from one metadata write,
  so a decode row gets the decode kernel whatever shares its step; CED decoder
  metadata takes the step kind and decode rows of the full-row metadata (the
  decode rows lead the decoder rows).

Decode-only steps are unchanged from the default path.
